// Rendered by modules/home/telegram.nix: @NAME@ placeholders are replaced with
// the active theme's colours and mixes (see .claude/rules/design.md).
// Telegram lays a theme over its default light palette, so every key that
// would otherwise show a light default is set here. A value may name another
// key instead of a colour.
//
// Design: neutral dark surfaces; the accent only for state (unread, links, ticks,
// send, focus, online). Outgoing bubbles are a soft accent tint with normal
// light text, never solid accent; the selected chat and folder are neutral grey.

